# What EAS Build uploads, and what it must not.
#
# EAS archives the project from the repository root. The first upload of Café Life was
# 829 MB: 397 MB of raw art sources and 306 MB of native/node_modules, none of which an iOS
# build uses. It meant a long upload for every cloud build, for nothing.
#
# Read this before editing: when this file exists, EAS ignores EVERY .gitignore in the
# repository, the nested ones too. Anything .gitignore used to keep out has to be
# restated here, or it ships. native/.gitignore is the one that matters.
#
# The app is native/ and nothing else. The game reaches it through
# native/src/webapp/html.js, which is committed and generated by tools/build-native.py,
# so the build needs neither the prototype nor the tools that produce it.

# --- every top-level folder that is not the app
/art/
/app/
/brand/
/design/
/design2/
/docs/
/prototype/
/tools/
/dist/
/site/
/.github/
/.venv/
# agents, and agent workspaces -- a workspace is a whole second copy of the repository.
# (No inline comments in this file: a trailing "# ..." becomes part of the pattern.)
/.claude/

# --- restated from native/.gitignore, which this file overrides
native/node_modules/
native/.expo/
native/ios/
native/android/

# --- restated from the root .gitignore
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.ipa
